# Changelog discipline

`CHANGELOG.md` follows [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/).

## Update it before committing

Any commit that touches user-visible behavior **must** update `CHANGELOG.md` first.
This includes: new features, bug fixes, CLI flag changes, config schema changes,
new man pages, release tooling, and documentation the user reads.

Pure internal refactors (test helpers, linter config, comment typos) may skip it,
but when in doubt, add an entry.

## Where to add entries

Unreleased work goes under the `## [Unreleased]` heading at the top.
Group entries under `### Added`, `### Changed`, `### Fixed`, or `### Removed`.

## What to write

One bullet per logical change. Lead with the artifact or command the user touches,
not with the implementation detail.

```
### Added
- `--no-update-check` flag and `TRIAGE_NO_UPDATE_CHECK=1` env var to suppress
  the release-staleness banner.
- Man pages `triage.1` and `triage.5` installed via Homebrew cask.

### Changed
- Homebrew install command is now `brew install --cask lolay/tap/triage`.
- `specs/config.md` is the canonical config reference; `specs/product.md §4–§5`
  now link there instead of duplicating content.
```

## Reminder for agents

Before calling `git commit`, check whether `CHANGELOG.md` appears in `git diff --name-only`.
If user-visible files changed and the changelog did not, add the entry first.
